*> PLB-C076 open-while-open: an OPEN of a file that an earlier OPEN
*> left open.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. OPENTWO.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT IN-FILE ASSIGN TO "in.dat".
    SELECT LOG-FILE ASSIGN TO "log.dat" FILE STATUS IS WS-LOG-STATUS.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  IN-FILE.
01  IN-REC              PIC X(80).
FD  LOG-FILE.
01  LOG-REC             PIC X(80).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-LOG-STATUS       PIC XX.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-PARA.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    READ IN-FILE
    *> Reported: the READ leaves the file open.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    CLOSE IN-FILE
    *> Not reported: CLOSE between.
    OPEN INPUT IN-FILE
    CLOSE IN-FILE
    *> Not reported: the status of the first OPEN is looked at.
    OPEN EXTEND LOG-FILE
    IF WS-LOG-STATUS = "35"
        OPEN OUTPUT LOG-FILE
    END-IF
    CLOSE LOG-FILE
    STOP RUN.
